-- `needs` coverage, TYPE DECLARATION positions, COVERED (2026-08-05).
--
-- Accept companion to reject/t148, t149 and t150: the same three shapes — a
-- record field, a variant argument, and a capability nested inside a
-- container — under a `needs` that covers them. All must typecheck.
--
-- This file carries a second, easily-missed requirement that the corpus
-- runner cannot express (it only checks exit status): these positions must
-- count as USES, so `needs` must not then report "declared but never used".
-- Otherwise fixing the error from t148 just trades it for a warning and the
-- check reads as broken. That silence is asserted in test_caps.ml; this file
-- pins the accept half.
--
-- `IO.FileSystem` covering both `IO.FileRead` and `IO.FileWrite` is
-- deliberate: it also proves lattice subsumption reaches the new positions
-- rather than requiring an exact string match on the declared capability.
mod CoveredDecls do
  needs IO.Console
  needs IO.FileSystem
  needs IO.NetConnect

  type Handle = { id : Int, tok : Cap(IO.FileWrite) }
  type Conn = Idle | Live(Cap(IO.NetConnect))
  type Bag = { label : String, items : List(Cap(IO.FileRead)) }

  fn main() do
    println("every capability named here is declared")
  end
end
